\f0\fs24 \cf0 # CXO Hive \'97 Research Rules\
\
## CORE OBJECTIVE\
\
Research daily content opportunities for CXO Hive.\
\
Maximize qualified ICP engagement. Build authority. Do not start by generating post ideas.\
\
Research first. Score second. Write opportunities, not posts.\
\
---\
\
## MANDATORY SEQUENCE\
\
Do this in order. Do not start with a keyword list.\
\
1. Read ICP, CXO Hive, Content Intelligence, and this file.\
2. Open the standing source map.\
3. Dig seed news outlets and seed LinkedIn accounts (ICP operators first, then adjacent creators).\
4. Collect phrases, tensions, and outlier posts.\
5. Hop: company/title-filtered LinkedIn, then commenters\'92 posts, then ICP reaction to the news.\
6. Keyword search only as a fallback, or to chase a newly discovered phrase.\
7. Score Stage 1, then Stage 2.\
8. Update the source map with new accounts, dead phrases, burned angles, and suspected engagement rings.\
\
If a scrape is blocked, retry with the other available tool. Do not score from a headline.\
\
---\
\
## RESEARCH PIPELINE\
\
1. Understand CXO Hive and the ICP.\
2. Research from the source map, then hop.\
3. Collect evidence.\
4. Stage 1 score. Keep roughly 20\'9640 findings if quality supports it. Do not force the number.\
5. Deduplicate. Keep source diversity.\
6. Stage 2 hard score.\
7. Select 5\'9610 final opportunities, or fewer if quality is weak.\
8. Output evidence-rich shortlist for human review.\
\
Two scoring stages. Do not collapse them.\
\
---\
\
## STAGE 1 \'97 FINDING SCORE\
\
Decide only: is this strong enough to enter the pool?\
\
Weights:\
\
- ICP Relevance \'97 25%\
- Evidence / Performance Strength \'97 25%\
- Topic / Idea Strength \'97 20%\
- ICP Engagement Quality \'97 15%\
- Freshness / Trend Potential \'97 10%\
- CXO Hive Relevance \'97 5%\
\
LinkedIn evidence: reactions, comments, reposts, impressions if available, engagement vs the author\'92s normal posts, comment quality, ICP participation.\
\
News/trends: evidence that people care. Do not invent performance.\
\
After scoring:\
\
- Drop duplicates, junk, and weak evidence.\
- Keep a mix of LinkedIn, ICP, creator, news, trend, CXO Hive, and experimental findings.\
- 60/20/10/10 is a guide. Quality overrides it.\
\
---\
\
## STAGE 2 \'97 HARD SCORE\
\
Decide: should this use a daily content slot?\
\
Score out of 100, then report /10.\
\
- ICP Resonance \'97 25%\
- Evidence of Attention \'97 20%\
- Idea / Topic Strength \'97 15%\
- Engagement Potential \'97 15%\
- Timeliness / Momentum \'97 10%\
- Differentiation / Gap \'97 10%\
- CXO Hive Credibility \'97 5%\
\
\'93Leadership\'94 is a weak idea. A specific tension can be a strong one.\
\
---\
\
## HARD SCORE REQUIREMENTS\
\
Be conservative.\
\
- 9.0+ = we would confidently consider publishing this.\
- 9.5 = unusually strong evidence, ICP relevance, and a usable angle.\
\
Do not give 9+ because the idea sounds interesting.\
Do not normalize scores upward.\
Most findings should not score 9+.\
\
A 9.0 requires qualified ICP engagement evidence, not only high reactions or a big news story.\
\
If nothing reaches 9.0, say so. Name the closest item and the missing evidence. Do not fill the list with eight 8s to look complete.\
\
---\
\
## SCORE CEILINGS\
\
- ICP Resonance < 7/10 \uc0\u8594  max 6.9\
- Evidence of Attention < 7/10 \uc0\u8594  max 7.4\
- Idea / Topic Strength < 7/10 \uc0\u8594  max 7.4\
- Engagement Potential < 6/10 \uc0\u8594  max 7.4\
- Generic, no differentiated angle \uc0\u8594  max 6.9\
- Unsupported claims \uc0\u8594  reject\
- One isolated weak signal \uc0\u8594  not high-confidence\
\
A news event with no ICP LinkedIn reaction \uc0\u8594  max 8.4\
High comments / reactions with low qualified ICP engagement \uc0\u8594  do not treat as 9.0\
\
---\
\
## QUALIFIED ICP ENGAGEMENT\
\
A reaction or comment counts as ICP evidence only if the person looks like the ICP: India-based, employed, mid-senior operator, relevant function, usually a large company.\
\
It does not count if they are a coach, trainer, recruiter, personal-brand seller, student, jobless, founder selling services, or a \'93DM me\'94 account.\
\
On any Stage 2 LinkedIn candidate, sample comments and visible reactor titles before scoring.\
\
- Prefer 30\'9650 comments on serious candidates, not 10.\
- Estimate an ICP-engager ratio. If it is weak, the post cannot be 9.0.\
- Compare performance to that author\'92s median. A journalist\'92s breaking-news post is not automatically exceptional.\
\
---\
\
## ENGAGEMENT RINGS\
\
The same handles or near-identical coach headlines appearing under multiple posts \'97 especially CXO Hive or lookalike coaches \'97 is a ring, not demand.\
\
Ring comments do not count as ICP evidence.\
High comment count + low unique ICP titles = distribution, not proof.\
\
CXO Hive\'92s own posts, and lookalike-coach posts, are calibration. They enter the final shortlist only if qualified ICP people are clearly in the engagement.\
\
---\
\
## SOURCE-SPECIFIC EVIDENCE\
\
### LinkedIn\
\
Use company and title filters before naked keyword search when the Actor allows it.\
\
Prioritize performance, comment quality, ICP participation, hook, format, recency, and whether this beat the author\'92s baseline.\
\
Preserve the source post and URL when used.\
If impressions are missing, write: Impressions unavailable. Do not estimate.\
\
### News / market\
\
Read named outlets in the source map first. Then find ICP reaction on LinkedIn.\
\
Prioritize recency, importance, ICP relevance, novelty, and whether it creates a real conversation.\
\
Do not treat an unpublished CXO Hive post as if the news \'93performed.\'94\
Do not state unconfirmed layoff or headcount numbers as fact.\
\
### ICP signal\
\
Repeated ICP behavior beats one comment.\
Language, questions, disagreement, and emotional intensity matter.\
\
### Creator pattern\
\
One viral post is not a pattern.\
A pattern needs repetition: topics, hooks, structures, or audience response across posts or creators.\
\
---\
\
## RESEARCH ADAPTATION\
\
Do not copy a source post.\
\
Source \uc0\u8594  why it worked \u8594  underlying idea \u8594  useful structure \u8594  what CXO Hive can add \u8594  original opportunity.\
\
The CXO Hive version may stay close to the idea. It must not be a rewrite of someone else\'92s post.\
\
When a new phrase appears, search that phrase, then check ICP engagement. Do not stay on the first query list.\
\
---\
\
## TOOLS\
\
### LinkedIn \'97 Apify MCP\
\
Use Apify when structured LinkedIn data is required.\
\
Do not hardcode one Actor forever. Inspect available Actors, read the schema, then run a targeted job.\
\
The question chooses the Actor. Do not scrape thousands of posts.\
\
Prefer:\
\
- posts from seed profiles\
- posts by people at ICP companies / with ICP titles\
- comments and reactors on shortlisted posts\
\
### News / web \'97 Firecrawl, then other web tools\
\
Use Firecrawl for search and article scrape when it is available and authenticated.\
\
If Firecrawl is unavailable, say so and use the next working web tool.\
\
LinkedIn stays on Apify. Do not scrape LinkedIn with Firecrawl.\
\
If a page is blocked or empty, retry with another fetch tool before giving up.\
\
---\
\
## EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE\
\
Separate:\
\
- FACT \'97 what the source states\
- OBSERVATION \'97 what repeats\
- INTERPRETATION \'97 what it may mean\
- HYPOTHESIS \'97 unproven\
\
Do not turn interpretation into fact.\
Do not say \'93this topic works\'94 when one post performed.\
\
Never invent metrics, impressions, reach, comments, quotes, testimonials, companies, outcomes, case studies, credentials, events, or trends.\
\
If it is not verified, mark it unavailable or insufficient.\
\
Prefer primary sources and original announcements for factual claims.\
Social posts are evidence of conversation, not proof of the event.\
\
---\
\
## FINAL OUTPUT\
\
Usually 5\'9610 opportunities. Fewer is fine. Do not pad.\
\
The shortlist should not be ten versions of one idea, unless one item is clearly exceptional.\
\
Each opportunity must include:\
\
1. Content opportunity\
2. Final score /10\
3. Evidence confidence \'97 HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW\
4. Source type\
5. Why the ICP cares\
6. Supporting evidence\
7. Source URL(s)\
8. What appears to be working\
9. Underlying idea\
10. CXO Hive opportunity / angle\
11. Suggested direction, hook, or format\
12. Risks, caveats, saturation\
\
LinkedIn-derived: author, URL, date, full post when appropriate, reactions, comments, reposts, impressions if available, ICP engagement evidence, why it worked, underlying idea.\
\
News/trend-derived: event, source, what happened, why it matters, ICP reason, current conversation, CXO Hive angle.\
\
Do not write the complete LinkedIn post unless asked.\
\
---\
\
## FINAL CHECK\
\
Reject or downgrade if any of these fail:\
\
- ICP would not care\
- Evidence is weak, invented, or ring-inflated\
- Idea is generic\
- News has no ICP conversation\
- One post is being treated as a market pattern\
- This is a topic, not an opportunity\
- It is not worth a daily slot\
\
The job is not to fill a quota.\
The job is to find the strongest opportunities in a large research space \'97 or to say the day did not produce one.}